35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The roster books are alarming. The late-turn pool is nearly empty, relying on overtime.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I found the pilots from eight years ago. The late-evening pilot actually met its cost-recovery target.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The committee minutes show the ferry and rail never agreed on data terms. That is a major blocker.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The ledger shows the operating subsidy was trimmed. The ticketing fees are higher than the paving budget.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"My audits confirm it. Most lost time is waiting for connections, not paying. The machines are fine.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, if the pilot worked, why did we not keep it? The staffing is the issue now.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the pilot worked, but the accessibility records show lane-priority failed. We need to be careful.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the data terms are missing. Any integrated plan will stall at the committee level.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, if waiting is the problem, does that mean we should focus on connections?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, yes. The timed runs show the surface route is slower, but the platforms clear fine.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts. That is a good sign for station upgrades.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,The accessibility records show four lifts finished on time. That is a strong precedent for station work.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The contingency pricing for pre-war shells is high. Station access upgrades will be expensive and risky.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"The ticketing fees are a drain. An integrated fare system might reduce those costs, but the data terms are missing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"If we fix the connections, we solve the waiting problem. The bus corridor might help with that.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am leaning towards station upgrades. The maintenance capacity is there, and the history is good.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I agree. The pilots show we can do this. The accessibility records prove we can finish on time.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am concerned about the pre-war shells. But the committee minutes suggest the data issue is specific to integration.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I am still worried about the budget. But if the ticketing fees are reduced, it might balance out.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I think station upgrades are the best bet. They address the real time loss and have a good track record.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
